// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO4-9 (ST7789P3 display SPI+control),
// GPIO11/12 (dedicated RTC I2C), GPIO40/41 (rotary encoder quadrature),
// GPIO46 (power-hold, internal-only) - confirmed via M5Stack DinMeter
// documentation. Encoder push-button(3), buzzer(42), and general Grove
// SDA/SCL(13/15) are kept.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO42 tagged "button" - confirmed vendor M5Unified library
// (M5Unified.cpp _begin(): case board_M5DinMeter sets GPIO_NUM_42 as input
// button/BtnA), corroborated by M5Stack Dial docs/ESPHome device page.
// This appears to contradict the older comment above (which says the
// button is GPIO3) - that older note looks swapped; left as-is per
// no-touch-existing-notes rule. See notes.txt for details.
